BaseScanner currently treats all circular includes as fatal.  This means when Follow #Includes when parsing working copies is enabled on the C/C++ preference page the model builder does not pick up class A when parsing a.h listed below.

This bug severely impacts one of our customers because they rely on our modeling tools which in turn require precise output from the model builder.

I've got a fix in the works which detects non-fatal circular includes and allows parsing to continue.

Doug can we spin another 3.1.2 build sometime this week to include this fix?

Thanks
Jason

-----8<----------

// a.h
#ifndef A_H_
#define A_H_
#include b.h
class A {}
#endif

-----8<----------

// b.h
#ifndef B_H_
#define B_H_
#include a.h
class B {}
#endif

