Static methods can't be overridden in Java. Nevertheless xtend requires to use the override keyword instead of def but creates valid Java code.

class A {
    def static hello() {
        println(hello A)
    }
}
class B extends A {
    def static hello() {        // *1
        println(hello B)
    }
}
class C extends A {
    override static hello() {   // *2
        println(hello C)
    }
}

*1 compile error in xtend file - but creates a correct B.java
*2 valid xtend but - isn't actually correct because A::hello() is not really overridden. But C.java is correct

